&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This internship provides hands-on exposure to &lt;strong&gt;Total Vehicle Engineering &lt;/strong&gt;within an advanced vehicle architecture and concept development environment. You will support early-phase platform engineering activities, evaluate emerging vehicle technologies, and contribute to rapid concept and prototype development across multiple vehicle systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;platform engineering, design, surfacing, HMI, and ergonomics&lt;/strong&gt;, offering a holistic view of how vehicles are conceived, packaged, and executed from concept to feasibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Daily Responsibilities of the Internship Program include&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;vehicle architecture and platform engineering &lt;/strong&gt;for future vehicle programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and benchmark &lt;strong&gt;new and emerging vehicle technologies &lt;/strong&gt;at the total-vehicle level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to &lt;strong&gt;rapid concept development and prototyping&lt;/strong&gt;, including CAD layouts and packaging studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with &lt;strong&gt;occupant packaging, ergonomics, and HMI layout&lt;/strong&gt;, balancing customer experience with engineering feasibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;exterior and interior surfacing activities&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring alignment between design intent and engineering criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and iterate &lt;strong&gt;3D CAD packaging proposals &lt;/strong&gt;to explore alternate architectural solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark competitive vehicle architectures using tools such as &lt;strong&gt;A2MAC1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support documentation of &lt;strong&gt;requirements, layouts, and design guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
