&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;Aurora’s mission is to deliver the benefits of self-driving technology safely, quickly, and broadly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;https://aurora.tech/aurora-driver&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://aurora.tech/aurora-driver&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;The Aurora Driver&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;will create a new era in mobility and logistics, one that will bring a safer, more efficient, and more accessible future to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;At Aurora, you will tackle massively complex problems alongside other passionate, intelligent individuals, growing as an expert while expanding your knowledge. For the latest news from Aurora, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://aurora.tech/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;aurora.tech&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;or follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/auroradriver&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Aurora hires talented people with diverse backgrounds who are ready to help build a transportation ecosystem that will make our roads safer, get crucial goods where they need to go, and make mobility more efficient and accessible for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re searching for a Software Engineer to join our Map Fusion team to develop algorithms that allow our vehicles to detect and respond to dynamic environmental changes like construction and emergency vehicles in real-time. This is an exciting opportunity to work at the intersection of &quot;classical&quot; geometric algorithms and modern machine learning to solve high-stakes, real-world safety challenges&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop onboard algorithms for updating map content in response to changing scenes such as construction zones and people directing traffic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement real-time compute solutions to update maps from sensor data on-the-fly while maintaining strict performance constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Motion Planning, Localization, and Fleet Intelligence teams to ensure seamless map integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to safety cases around modern machine learning methods to ensure rigorous safety standards are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize graph-centric and geometric algorithms to produce the local geometry of lane lines and driveable surfaces used by the motion planning system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in C++ with a focus on building functional, production level software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python for algorithm development and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong 3D geometric reasoning skills to handle complex mapping data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of graph theory, including practical applications of algorithms like Dijkstra’s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Deep Learning methods and their application to real-world data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Bayesian Inference for probabilistic reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Spline Manipulation for geometric path and surface modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in autonomous vehicle technology or related high-performance computing industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
